  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.S.Assees vs The Muvattupuzha Municipality on 13 December, 2024 Wp(C) No.43415/2024 1/4 Order Date : 13-12-2 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice Ziyad Rahman A.A. Friday, the 13th day of December 2024 / 22nd Agrahayana, 1946 Wp(C) No. 43415 Of 2024 Petitioner: A.S.Assees,Aged 65 Years, S/O J.K.Saidali (Late), Ambadan House, Kanjirakkad, Rayonpuram P.O., Perumbavoor, Ernakulam District., Pin - 683543 Respondents: 1. The Muvattupuzha Municipality, Municipal Office, Muvattupuzha Old Bridge Rd, Thottumkalpeedika, Muvattupuzha,Ernakulam District, Represented By Its Secretary,Pin - 686673 2. The Secretary, Muvattupuzha Municipality, Municipal Office, Muvattupuzha Old Bridge Rd, Thottumkalpeedika, Muvattupuzha,Ernakulam District., Pin - 686673 3. THE DISTRICT TRANSPORT OFFICER, KERALA STATE ROAD TRANSPORT CORPORATION, MUVATTUPUZHA P.O., ERNAKULAM DISTRICT., PIN - 686673 Writ petition (civil) praying inter alia that in the circumstances stated in the affidavit filed along with the WP(C) the High Court be pleased to direct the 2nd respondent to take immediate steps to remove the shed which was constructed illegally and to stop the functioning of the shed without license in the waiting area provided for the passengers in the KSRTC Bus Stand Building at Muvattupuzha by implementing Exhibits P-2 and P-3 forthwith, pending disposal of the writ petition. This petition coming on for orders upon perusing the petition and the affidavit filed in support of WP(C) and upon hearing the arguments of M/S.SAJEEV KUMAR K.GOPAL, ANN SUSAN GEORGE, ASWATHY BABU & GOPIKA S. NAIR Advocates for the petitioner, SRI.T.R.RAJAN, STANDING COUNSEL for the respondents 1 & 2 and of M/S. RAJAN T.R. & P.C.CHACKO Advocates for the respondent 3, the court passed the following: WP(C) No.43415/2024 2/4 Ord ZIYAD RAHMAN A.A., J. ======================== W.P(C) No.43415 of 2024 ======================== A.S.Assees vs The Muvattupuzha Municipality on 13 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/149423866/ 1 Dated this the 13th day of December, 2024 ORDER Admit. 2.",
    "facts": "3. The reliefs sought in the writ petition is to direct the 2 nd respondent to remove the shed wherein a tea shop is being conducted in the KSRTC bus stand. 3. Considering the fact that, the petitioner herein is conducting a tea shop on the basis of Ext.P1 agreement executed between the petitioner WP(C) No.43415/2024 3/4 Order Date : 13-12-2024 and the KSRTC and also that, the petitioner has obtained Ext.P4 from the Department of Industries and Commerce, under Kerala Micro Small Medium Enterprises Facilitation Rules, 2020 to set up a service enterprise, I am inclined to pass an interim order. Moreover, the petitioner has also obtained Ext.P5 license from the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India as well.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
